{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "spec-gate-before-apply",
  "description": "Before executing a spec task, verifies compliance with The Sixbell-Dev Way by checking that all mandatory governance items are present in the spec.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "preTaskExecution"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A spec task is about to be executed. Before proceeding, verify compliance with The Sixbell-Dev Way using the official OpenSpec structure.\n\nCheck that the following mandatory items are satisfied:\n\n1. There is an active change under `openspec/changes/<change-name>/`\n2. `proposal.md` exists and the objective/scope is explicit\n3. Relevant delta specs exist under the change when behavior or workflow is changing, or there is a clear explanation for why no delta spec is required\n4. `design.md` exists when required by the repository's schema and the implementation approach is explicit\n5. `review.md` exists and identifies risk, security impact, cost/operational impact, rollback or migration considerations, and approval status\n6. `tasks.md` exists and aligns with the approved review outcome\n7. Explicit human approval exists\n8. The relationship to current source-of-truth specs under `openspec/specs/` is clear\n9. Documentation impact has been identified\n\nIf any mandatory item is missing:\n\n- Classify it as **blocking** (must be resolved before execution can proceed) or **warning** (should be addressed but does not prevent execution)\n- Explain clearly what is missing and why it matters\n- If the issue is classified as blocking, DO NOT proceed with the task — stop progress and inform the user what needs to be resolved first\n\nIf all items are satisfied, confirm compliance and allow the task to proceed."
  },
  "shortName": "spec-gate-before-apply"
}
